{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792945590,"nonce":"4ZFZJAsRpS9lrgEHHpNIeyErFHk=","message":"Browser client (web/session, commit 33f1118): a local-first client over Yjs and IndexedDB that reconnects with backoff, runs the state-vector handshake for every open document after each (re)connect, holds edits while signed out, and sends them after `auth.login`. A demo page (file list, textarea bound to a document, sign-in banner) is its harness. Three headless-Chromium tests pass against the Rust server: typing reaches the file and a file edit reaches the page; edits made while the server is down survive in IndexedDB, through a closed page, and reach the file when the server returns; nothing is sent before sign-in and the typed edit goes after it. npm is used only to bundle and test the browser client; the session is Rust.\n\nNot done: the Workspace interface in RayDE (Haxe) and the page agent that carries the socket to the Ash program; RayDE has not been run in a page yet. `ash --build` of today's RayDE links (7661/7661 functions, 33.6 MB with fibers) but the ashui page staging (blinc_abi.wasm, xgpu.wasm, xwindow.wasm) has not been wired for RayDE, so there are no in-page measurements yet.","files":null}]}